.TH "FLORENCE" "1" "July 24, 2026" "Florence 0.7.0" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
florence \- extensible scalable virtual keyboard for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B florence
[\fIOPTION\fR ...] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARG\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B florence
is an extensible, scalable virtual keyboard for X11.
You need it if you cannot use a hardware keyboard, for example because
of injury, handicap, a broken keyboard, or because you use a tablet or
convertible with a touchscreen, but you are able to use a pointing
device such as a mouse, a trackball, a stylus, or a touchscreen.
.PP
Florence stays out of your way when you do not need it: it can be
configured to appear on the screen only when needed.
A timer-based auto-click input method is available to help people who
have difficulty clicking, and the ramble mode provides an efficient
gesture-based input method.
.PP
Keyboard layouts are rendered from scalable SVG artwork and may define
additional layers, including an
.B Fn
layer providing XF86 multimedia and brightness keys.
Layout extensions can add or remove key rows, and the keyboard may be
resized freely.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the Florence version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config
Open the configuration window.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug " [\fILEVEL\fR]"
Launch Florence in verbose mode, printing debug information to standard
output.
An optional level selects the verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-debounce " \fITIME\fR"
Set the focus event debounce time, in milliseconds (default 10).
This prevents input bounce with some applications.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-focus " [\fIWINDOW\fR]"
Send all Florence input to the selected window.
The window argument is the name of the window, as most window managers
display in the title bar; when omitted, Florence selects the last
focused window.
This option is useful under window managers that do not support the
.I not focusable
hint and would otherwise focus the keyboard window instead of the
output window.
It must be used for the keyboard to work in a display manager greeter.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-use\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Use the given configuration file instead of dconf.
The configuration file is a key-value pair file with sections.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-greeter
Greeter mode, for use on a display manager login screen such as
.BR xdm (1) :
the preferences dialog and menu are disabled, and a safer key glyph set
is used.
.SH COMMANDS
When a running Florence instance exists, the following commands control
it and then exit:
.TP
.B show
Show the keyboard.
.TP
.B hide
Hide the keyboard.
.TP
.B move \fIx\fR,\fIy\fR
Move the keyboard to position \fIx\fR,\fIy\fR on the screen.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored under the
.B org.florence
GSettings schema and may be edited with the configuration window
.RB ( "florence \-c" ),
with
.BR dconf (1)
tooling, or supplied as a flat file with the
.B \-\-use\-config
option.
.SH SEE ALSO
Florence project page:
.I https://github.com/FrauBSD/florence
.SH AUTHORS
Florence was written by François Agrech <f.agrech@gmail.com>.
.PP
